  {
    "annotations": {
      "description": "Bee's calls to its Gnosis RPC endpoint are failing at a sustained rate. The chain-reading endpoints degrade first \u2014 /api/v1/wallet, /api/v1/chequebook/balance and /chainstate start returning \"Failed to fetch ... from Swarm API\" \u2014 while the rest of the gateway keeps working, so overall status stays green.\n\nWhat to check, in order:\n1. Which endpoint this node uses: BEE_RPC_ENDPOINT (main) or BEE_DEV_RPC_ENDPOINT (development) in /opt/swarm_connect_host.env on the host.\n2. Whether both nodes point at the same endpoint. They share a public IP, so one endpoint means one rate limit, and staging load will break production. That was swarm_connect#296.\n3. The node's log for the actual refusal: docker logs --since 1h <container> | grep -E '429|502|503|504'\n\nIgnore this if the node restarted in the last few minutes \u2014 it hammers the endpoint catching up and a burst of errors then is expected.\n\nFull status: {{ if eq $labels.environment \"main\" }}https://provenance-gateway.datafund.io/health{{ else if eq $labels.environment \"development\" }}https://provenance-gateway.dev.datafund.io/health{{ else }}https://provenance-gateway.datafund.io/health (or the .dev. host \u2014 environment label was \"{{ $labels.environment }}\"){{ end }}",
      "summary": "Gnosis RPC error rate {{ printf \"%.1f\" $values.C.Value }}% on {{ $labels.environment }} (sustained over 15m)"
    },
    "condition": "D",
    "data": [
      {
        "datasourceUid": "grafanacloud-prom",
        "model": {
          "expr": "100 * sum(rate(bee_eth_backend_total_rpc_errors[10m])) by (environment) / sum(rate(bee_eth_backend_total_rpc_calls[10m])) by (environment)",
          "instant": true,
          "intervalMs": 1000,
          "maxDataPoints": 43200,
          "refId": "A"
        },
        "queryType": "",
        "refId": "A",
        "relativeTimeRange": {
          "from": 900,
          "to": 0
        }
      },
